  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry conditions and seasonable temperatures \nexpected this weekend and into next week. \n\nDry high pressure will build across the Southeast United States this \nweekend and prevail through early next week. Cold air advection post \nfropa will set the stage for noticeably cooler temps today and \nSunday, although are expected to remain above normal for afternoon \nhighs, generally in the mid-upper 70s this afternoon, then low-mid \n70s Sunday afternoon. Overnight periods will feature cooler temps as \nwell while high pressure settles across the area, sfc winds become \nrather light, and a fair amount of radiational cooling takes place \nunder more substantial clearing. In general, temps should dip \ninto the mid 40s inland to mid-upper 50s near the coast tonight,\nthen a few degrees cooler Sunday night. \n\nHigh pressure will reside across the Southeast early into the middle \nof next week, setting the stage for rebounding temps as a west flow \nbecomes more pronounced across the local area. In general, afternoon \nhighs should return to the mid-upper 70s. However, light winds and \nradiational cooling nights will continue to support lows in the low-\nmid 40s inland to low-mid 50s near coastal areas into the middle of \nnext week.",
